From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <oliversargisonb@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:41:34 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 42/51] Plutonium: preview recordings are captures every shell
 sees

preview_recording_start on a tab Plutonium's helper shows registers the
recording with the helper (the channel's "recording" command), which makes
it a capture with no node: every shell gets capturestart and can stop it,
and the recording switch refuses it, which fails the start with the
switch's reason. A shell's stop ("ended") stops the screencast;
preview_recording_stop still returns what was recorded. T3's own encoder
and pointer drawing stay as they are.
